WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.428 --> 00:00:02.246
When contact goes unnoticed,

2
00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.627
a routine placement can tip a cup.

3
00:00:04.942 --> 00:00:06.535
In these example trials,

4
00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:10.575
CoPRE retreats, while the neural baseline keeps moving.

5
00:00:12.383 --> 00:00:15.883
CoPRE detects weak contact using proprioception:

6
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.792
the robot's built in joint and motor signals.

7
00:00:20.377 --> 00:00:22.997
Weak contact produces small torque changes.

8
00:00:23.324 --> 00:00:24.970
These can be hidden by friction,

9
00:00:25.153 --> 00:00:28.405
motion, and noise in the robot's built in signals.

10
00:00:30.387 --> 00:00:32.900
We train a separate predictor for each robot

11
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:34.744
using contact free motion,

12
00:00:35.031 --> 00:00:38.599
then calibrate the detection threshold on separate recordings.

13
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.619
Nominal torque is the torque expected without contact.

14
00:00:43.933 --> 00:00:47.303
We predict it from earlier states and known commands,

15
00:00:47.578 --> 00:00:50.948
excluding recent observations that may reflect contact.

16
00:00:52.275 --> 00:00:54.316
A noise weighted Jacobian combines

17
00:00:54.316 --> 00:00:56.451
observed minus predicted torque,

18
00:00:56.625 --> 00:00:58.684
giving noisier joints less weight.

19
00:00:59.036 --> 00:01:00.808
Three consecutive contact scores

20
00:01:00.808 --> 00:01:03.416
at or above threshold confirm contact.

21
00:01:04.378 --> 00:01:06.827
We measure reference sliding resistance:

22
00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.827
the force needed to start each book stack sliding.

23
00:01:12.381 --> 00:01:15.355
Each arm is tested at five reference resistances

24
00:01:15.355 --> 00:01:17.041
and three pushing speeds,

25
00:01:17.249 --> 00:01:19.133
with three repetitions per condition.

26
00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:21.926
On the G1 humanoid,

27
00:01:22.054 --> 00:01:24.934
detection uses only the right arm's signals,

28
00:01:25.049 --> 00:01:27.372
with its own predictor and calibration.

29
00:01:28.435 --> 00:01:31.621
Recall is the percentage of contact trials detected.

30
00:01:31.935 --> 00:01:35.832
CoPRE reaches seventy four point one percent on ARX

31
00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:38.489
and eighty two point two percent on G1,

32
00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.369
exceeding both baselines

33
00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:42.976
under each robot's evaluation protocol.

34
00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.849
At three point five newtons for ARX

35
00:01:46.849 --> 00:01:48.743
and five point five for G1,

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:50.683
detection reaches ninety percent

37
00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.397
and stays above it at higher tested resistances.

38
00:01:54.388 --> 00:01:56.692
Contact feedback also guides action.

39
00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:59.416
Here, a cup blocks the planned placement.

40
00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:03.097
The robot retreats and chooses a new placement.

41
00:02:05.382 --> 00:02:07.936
It places the block at an alternate location,

42
00:02:08.224 --> 00:02:09.410
leaving the cup upright.

43
00:02:13.379 --> 00:02:16.972
Next, the robot inserts a book beside neighboring books.

44
00:02:19.379 --> 00:02:21.090
Contact with a neighboring book

45
00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:23.578
prompts the robot to adjust its pose.

46
00:02:25.388 --> 00:02:28.166
The robot adjusts its approach and retries,

47
00:02:28.349 --> 00:02:31.403
guided by contact feedback and task progress.

48
00:02:33.388 --> 00:02:35.403
The book enters the available gap

49
00:02:35.506 --> 00:02:36.916
and is seated in the shelf.

50
00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.335
Contact feedback helps the robot

51
00:02:39.335 --> 00:02:41.442
adapt its motion during insertion.

52
00:02:45.391 --> 00:02:47.945
The gripper releases the book and withdraws.

53
00:02:50.385 --> 00:02:52.902
CoPRE improves weak contact sensitivity

54
00:02:52.965 --> 00:02:54.553
on two robot platforms.

55
00:02:54.811 --> 00:02:57.443
Its contact feedback supports protective retreat

56
00:02:57.564 --> 00:02:59.140
and book insertion retries.
